That story's made-up, isn't it?

234
00:14:08,138 --> 00:14:10,765
That's how much buying
a comic book store means to me.

235
00:14:14,311 --> 00:14:16,604
I'd like your honest opinion on something.

236
00:14:16,772 --> 00:14:18,440
Of course.

237
00:14:18,607 --> 00:14:23,107
Now, before I start, I need you to know
that I'm very excited about this.

238
00:14:23,445 --> 00:14:27,574
And anything you say
that isn't enthusiastically supportive...

239
00:14:27,741 --> 00:14:31,995
...will throw our entire relationship
into question.

240
00:14:33,914 --> 00:14:37,876
So keep an open mind.

241
00:14:38,502 --> 00:14:40,879
I'm feeling a little backed into a corner,
Sheldon.

242
00:14:41,380 --> 00:14:42,756
Perfect.

243
00:14:44,383 --> 00:14:48,883
Now, I'm considering investing
in Stuart's comic book store.

244
00:14:50,430 --> 00:14:51,556
Interesting.

245
00:14:54,226 --> 00:14:58,726
Can you see how a grown man,
an accomplished scientist...

246
00:14:58,939 --> 00:15:03,439
...who invests in a store that sells picture
books about flying men in colorful underwear...

247
00:15:07,447 --> 00:15:11,284
...might be wasting both his financial
and intellectual resources?

248
00:15:18,375 --> 00:15:19,876
No.

249
00:15:22,254 --> 00:15:24,464
Then I think it's a terrific idea.

250
00:15:25,424 --> 00:15:26,550
Great.

251
00:15:26,716 --> 00:15:29,385
Wait till you hear about our van.

252
00:15:31,847 --> 00:15:33,849
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

253
00:15:35,100 --> 00:15:38,645
-Hey. Thanks for inviting us over.
-Hi. Thank you for coming.

254
00:15:38,812 --> 00:15:40,688
Listen, Penny, before you start...

255
00:15:40,856 --> 00:15:43,984
...I wanna apologize for being so rude
the other day in my office.

256
00:15:44,192 --> 00:15:47,195
-No, no. No need to apologize.
-Excuse me, can I say something?

257
00:15:47,362 --> 00:15:51,366
I just love both you guys
and I want you to get along.

258
00:15:51,533 --> 00:15:53,701
And when I say "love," I meant as a friend.

259
00:15:55,412 --> 00:15:57,455
And, uh, we're too soon, right?

260
00:15:59,207 --> 00:16:00,666
Okay, sit down. Listen, Emily...

261
00:16:00,834 --> 00:16:03,711
...what happened between me and Raj
was a long time ago.

262
00:16:03,879 --> 00:16:06,339
I made it seem like
a bigger deal than I should have.

263
00:16:06,506 --> 00:16:08,382
Yeah. And Leonard and I are engaged now.

264
00:16:08,550 --> 00:16:11,219
And I'm just hoping
we can put this whole thing behind us.

265
00:16:11,386 --> 00:16:12,720
I'd like that too.

266
00:16:12,888 --> 00:16:16,474
Yeah, I thought I'd be okay with it,
but then I saw how pretty you are.

267
00:16:16,683 --> 00:16:20,228
Oh. That's so sweet.
I mean, look at you, you are gorgeous.

268
00:16:20,729 --> 00:16:23,231
It's true, you're both gorgeous.

269
00:16:24,232 --> 00:16:26,609
Kind of says something about the man
who could bed you both.

270
00:16:26,776 --> 00:16:28,903
[CHUCKLES]

271
00:16:34,576 --> 00:16:37,245
You get why I've been alone
most of my adult life.

272
00:16:40,248 --> 00:16:42,124
So, what brings you by?

273
00:16:42,292 --> 00:16:45,628
Well, I don't need a reason, it's my house.

274
00:16:45,795 --> 00:16:50,295
Technically it's your mom's house,
but we certainly want you to feel welcome.

275
00:16:51,468 --> 00:16:53,636
I'm always welcome.

276
00:16:54,262 --> 00:16:56,514
Just try and call first.

277
00:16:57,390 --> 00:17:00,267
Okay, let's get down to business.

278
00:17:00,435 --> 00:17:03,896
Howie was thinking about putting up
some money to help reopen the store...

279
00:17:04,064 --> 00:17:07,067
...but before that happens,
I have a few questions.

280
00:17:07,317 --> 00:17:11,446
I appreciate the offer, but actually,
your mother already gave me the money.

281
00:17:13,823 --> 00:17:15,324
What?

282
00:17:16,284 --> 00:17:20,784
Yeah. I told her it was too much, but she said
she was happy to help out her bubala.

283
00:17:20,956 --> 00:17:22,165
[CHUCKLES]

284
00:17:23,291 --> 00:17:24,792
Excuse me.

285
00:17:25,460 --> 00:17:27,879
Ma, you are canceling that check...

286
00:17:28,046 --> 00:17:32,546
...and Stuart is not your bubala, I'm your
bubala, you can't have more than one bubala!

287
00:17:34,344 --> 00:17:37,805
I don't know who he's talking to,
she's at Target buying me shirts.

288
00:17:41,226 --> 00:17:43,519
I'm so glad we could work this all out.

289
00:17:43,687 --> 00:17:45,313
Yeah, me too.

290
00:17:45,480 --> 00:17:47,523
We should have dinner
with you and Leonard.

291
00:17:47,691 --> 00:17:49,442
-We would love that.
-Great.

292
00:17:50,735 --> 00:17:52,695
-Okay, good night, guys.
-All right, night.

293
00:17:52,862 --> 00:17:54,488
Bye.

294
00:17:55,115 --> 00:17:56,991
BOTH:
I hate her.

295
00:18:02,789 --> 00:18:05,917
I'm disappointed we're not gonna have
our own comic book store.

296
00:18:06,084 --> 00:18:07,668
I was looking forward to it.

297
00:18:07,836 --> 00:18:10,088
Would have been nice
to have a place that's ours.

298
00:18:10,255 --> 00:18:12,924
Where we could just sit
and read comics in peace.

299
00:18:13,091 --> 00:18:14,383
With comfy seats.

300
00:18:14,551 --> 00:18:15,802
And snacks.

301
00:18:15,969 --> 00:18:17,929
I guess it was too good to be true.

302
00:18:18,096 --> 00:18:19,680
Yeah.

303
00:18:20,515 --> 00:18:22,517
[ALL SIGH]

304
00:18:49,836 --> 00:18:51,838
[English - US - SDH]

